            <ArticleTitle>ST segment and T wave abnormalities not caused by acute coronary syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-111, vi</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the ST segment and T wave abnormalities seen in non-acute coronary syndrome (ACS) electrocardiograph presentations. Particular emphasis is placed on the distinction of these non-ACS syndromes from acute coronary syndrome related ST segment and or T wave change.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
